{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/689324-some-questions-about-vampire-powers","id":689324,"title":"Some questions about vampire powers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-04T22:45:24-07:00","id":689324,"title":"Some questions about vampire powers","content":"If a vampire has Protean 4, the Claws Of The Unholy Merit, Vigor 5 and uses all at once, does he get a Damage Bonus of +5A and Armor Piercing 2? Wouldn't that make the Cruac power called Feedind The Crone from the 1ED core book seem inferior?<br /> <br /> Is there an upper limit to the dice bonus granted by Phyical Intensity? Could a vampire with Blood Potency 7 spend 7 Vitae to get +14 , or should it cap at +10?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T23:28:52-07:00","id":689361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/689324-some-questions-about-vampire-powers#post689324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a vampire has Protean 4, the Claws Of The Unholy Merit, Vigor 5 and uses all at once, does he get a Damage Bonus of +5A and Armor Piercing 2?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it keeps the armor piercing, but I'm not positive on that one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/689324-some-questions-about-vampire-powers#post689324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't that make the Cruac power called Feedind The Crone from the 1ED core book seem inferior?</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's a bigger aggravated damage modifier, but it requires 36 experiences worth of traits for a Gangrel (35 experiences for a Daeva or Nosferatu, 40 for anyone else), requires you to be in frenzy to use it, and costs 1 Vitae to activate Unnatural Aspect plus 1 more for each hit to activate Vigor. Versus Feeding the Crone which only costs 16 experiences if you take it as your free ritual for buying the 4th dot of Cruac (18 if you buy it separately), and only costs 1 Vitae to activate, and lasts until the next sunrise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/689324-some-questions-about-vampire-powers#post689324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there an upper limit to the dice bonus granted by Phyical Intensity? Could a vampire with Blood Potency 7 spend 7 Vitae to get +14 , or should it cap at +10?</div> </div> </div> </div>+14. As long as you can spend the Vitae, you get the full bonus. That's a lot of Vitae to spend just to boost one roll though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-05-2015, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T06:16:45-07:00","id":689627,"title":"","content":"Considering that Feeding the Crone takes about half an hour to set up, stops you feeding and takes a vitae to dismiss before dawn so you need to make sure you save one or you'll starve into torpor I'm not sure it's the lack of damage that makes Feeding the Crone seem inferior. I think <i>actually being inferior</i> does that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T10:11:35-07:00","id":689855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/689324-some-questions-about-vampire-powers?p=689627#post689627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that Feeding the Crone takes about half an hour to set up, stops you feeding and takes a vitae to dismiss before dawn so you need to make sure you save one or you'll starve into torpor I'm not sure it's the lack of damage that makes Feeding the Crone seem inferior. I think <i>actually being inferior</i> does that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but again it's less than half of the exp cost and you don't have to drink another vampire's blood to learn it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T10:17:35-07:00","id":689875,"title":"","content":"Actually, couldn't you use vigor with Feeding the Crone anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T10:46:31-07:00","id":689900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/689324-some-questions-about-vampire-powers?p=689875#post689875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, couldn't you use vigor with Feeding the Crone anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. And 4 dots of Cruac costs the same amount as 4 dots of Protean and a 4 dot Merit for Gangrel, 4 less for anyone else.<br /> <br /> Although in that case, you'd probably want to drop the effect after a scene so you can feed to refill on all the Vitae you spent on Vigor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}